    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pho bo is a Vietnamese beef noodle soup famous for its clear, spiced broth. The key technique is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "char-aromatics"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "charring the aromatics "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". blackening the onion and ginger before they go into the pot gives the broth colour and depth without cloudiness. This recipe serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Blanch the bones first to remove impurities . this is what keeps the broth clear. The spices go in whole and are strained out at the end."
          }
        ]
      },
